 {"t_ms": 53425, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01TQBkQqAAkLCbNn5U5Pf1T9", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 53425, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01TQBkQqAAkLCbNn5U5Pf1T9", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 54845, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01HP3GRzNiu9HkFZB8La5cbq", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55145, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01HP3GRzNiu9HkFZB8La5cbq", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55145, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01HP3GRzNiu9HkFZB8La5cbq", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 59751, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n1. **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy. v2.3.1 (the current release) and its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, were both unhealthy. Before the rollback, all regions were on v2.3.1 with an error rate of about 18%.\n2. **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error. That left us-east on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west stayed on v2.3.1. I retried once, and it finished in every region. us-east, us-west and eu-west are now all on v2.3.0, and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n3. **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so there's no duplicate. It's **INC-0001** (SEV2, checkout-api), and it pages the on-call engineer. It covers why v2.3.1 failed, the rollback including the partial failure, the current state, and two follow-ups: finding out why v2.3.1 failed and why the orchestrator stopped the first rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Xc53Jsk23drfT1dkCE6eFE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01R2G5akNuNxdEHj6tHx3me2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01F51nLoBtpDKV3z3UeJDFjt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_019sfZuiaJEi14ztPEJhgvVU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway through: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version again should be safe to repeat, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01L8XJ3hVipPNhS8vE6VUBur", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Jryhban8QisZjsH9GMChsr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01U4N4f2ZCHmNgnPhWC5E7ge", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01TQBkQqAAkLCbNn5U5Pf1T9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the latest deploy, checkout-api v2.3.1 failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy. We rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt failed partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, which left the regions on mixed versions (us-east v2.3.0, us-west/eu-west v2.3.1). A second attempt finished in all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, service healthy, error rate about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01HP3GRzNiu9HkFZB8La5cbq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n1. **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy. v2.3.1 (the current release) and its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, were both unhealthy. Before the rollback, all regions were on v2.3.1 with an error rate of about 18%.\n2. **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error. That left us-east on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west stayed on v2.3.1. I retried once, and it finished in every region. us-east, us-west and eu-west are now all on v2.3.0, and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n3. **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so there's no duplicate. It's **INC-0001** (SEV2, checkout-api), and it pages the on-call engineer. It covers why v2.3.1 failed, the rollback including the partial failure, the current state, and two follow-ups: finding out why v2.3.1 failed and why the orchestrator stopped the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}